// Fixture for cratestack#407's Dart-client verification: a single
// procedure declaring `@status(202)`, mirroring
// `crates/cratestack-client/tests/fixtures/status_override.cstack` (the
// already-proven Rust-client fixture) so the two generated clients are
// tested against the exact same schema shape. The point is settling the
// issue's still-open half of the client-generator question: does the
// generated Dart client (default preset AND riverpod preset, both of
// which talk HTTP directly via `dio` — no Rust FFI bridge involved) treat
// a bare `202` response as success, or does it silently require exactly
// `200`?

procedure submit(args: SubmitArgs): SubmitReply
  @status(202)

type SubmitArgs {
  message String
}

type SubmitReply {
  echo String
}
